================================================================================
WRONGFUL USE WARNING
================================================================================

This notice is a condition of use, not legal advice. Read it before running
anything in this repository.

This software archives other people's private conversations. That is its
entire function. The messages it collects were written by real people who did
not agree to have them stored, indexed, searched, exported, or fed into a
machine learning model. Treat every message you collect as something you are
holding on someone else's behalf.

WHAT THIS SOFTWARE IS FOR

  Archiving and searching conversations you are a legitimate party to, or that
  you have permission to retain — your own message history, a community you
  administer with the knowledge of its members, or research with informed
  consent and an ethics review.

WHAT YOU MUST NOT USE THIS SOFTWARE FOR

  - Surveillance, stalking, monitoring, or building a profile of any person.
  - Harassment, intimidation, blackmail, doxxing, or exposing private
    conversation, whether or not you were part of it.
  - Collecting messages from minors, or from any space you gained access to
    under false pretenses, through a compromised account, or by evading a
    ban, block, or permission setting.
  - Training, fine-tuning, or prompting a model to imitate a specific real
    person without that person's explicit, informed, revocable consent.
  - Republishing, selling, leaking, or otherwise redistributing collected
    messages, including as a "dataset."
  - Any purpose that would be unlawful, tortious, or harmful if done by hand
    instead of by script.

LEGAL EXPOSURE IS YOURS ALONE

  Automating a user account against Discord's API violates the Discord Terms
  of Service and can get your account permanently terminated. Depending on
  where you and the people you collect from live, mass collection and
  retention of private messages may also engage data-protection law (such as
  the GDPR or CCPA), wiretap and interception statutes, computer-misuse law,
  and civil liability for invasion of privacy.

  You are solely responsible for how you use this software and for everything
  you collect with it. The author provides no warranty, does not endorse any
  particular use, and accepts no liability for any harm, loss, claim, or
  penalty arising from your use of it — as stated in the MIT terms above.

IF YOU COLLECT ANYTHING, LOOK AFTER IT

  The database this tool creates contains your Discord token in plaintext
  alongside every message you have scraped. Keep it local, keep it encrypted
  if you can, never commit it to version control, and delete it when you no
  longer need it. If you are not prepared to be a careful custodian of other
  people's words, do not run this.
